From 70f362e2e262a64e3edf3bfebc84f7dcc268c8e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:12:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] hub admission: the hub judges a foreign hub-bound
 card at pickup; dispatch refuses an unjudged copy

Problem: 11-12 10:55Z worker-4 created t_01a1cf65a941bf43 with runs_on=["machine:hub"] and no
hub_admission verdict (created payload or event); at 10:58Z the hub's pickup copied and claimed it.
Over the prior 7 days the hub claimed 8 foreign cards pinned machine:hub, 0 with any verdict.
Why 1: the creator computed placement locally on a core older than the admission gate (abec81ec81).
Why 2: pool-worker core updates were deferred for hours (worker-1 still on 4c34063355), so creators
  run without the gate.
Root (happened): admission ran only on the creating host; kanban_worker_node.pickup copied and claimed
  any card whose runs_on only the hub could satisfy, with no verdict check.
Root (not caught): no test covered a foreign card that reaches the hub without a verdict; every
  admission test exercised the creator's own entry points.

Fix:
- hermes_cli/kanban_hub_admission_pickup.screen runs before import_cards on the hub. A card only the
  hub can claim (hub_bound: machine:<hub>, or labels no active worker carries) without an admit
  verdict is judged outside any write transaction. Admitted: copied, hub_admission event (entry
  pickup). Denied: copied to record the verdict, re-placed on the hub's worker_queue via the
  creation-time deny route (pool_route; hub:write added for a home-gateway marker) with a moved event
  citing it; never claimed here. Structural or no worker queue: verdict recorded, left pinned,
  never re-judged on that placement. Unavailable judge: not copied, pickup-skip reason, retried
  next tick; one outage per tick, not one timeout per card.
- dispatch_refusals (local_refusals) refuses a foreign hub-bound copy with no admit verdict
  (hub_admission_missing), so no other import path can claim one.

Proof: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_hub_admission_pickup.py (14 tests) RED on main for the pickup
and dispatch cases; 24/24 condition mutants killed (screen/apply/backstop unwiring, verdict reuse,
re-judge on a new placement, in-transaction and one-outage guards, hub_bound rules, refusal
scope). 36 related kanban files, 716 tests pass. Replay against the hub's live board: 6 open
foreign machine:hub cards lack a verdict (2 ready, 2 running, 2 scheduled: e.g. "Land myapp
branch ..." and "Build the serialized land lane ..."); the ready/scheduled ones will be judged at
their next pickup, running ones are not touched.
